  "model": "EP-133 K.O. II",
  "category": "sampler",
  "summary": "A pocket sampler and composer with a built-in microphone, twelve pads across nine groups, and a punch-in effects section. Every socket is along its top edge, so it has a face you play and a top you patch, and no back at all. Drawn looking down at it: the pad grid, the number keys and the display are the surface, and the five sockets run along its back edge - the top edge as you look down at it, which is what the entry used to call it. The key and pad counts are the arrangement rather than a census. Its twelve sample pads send notes from 36 on channel 10.",
